dbt2dataform reimplements behaviour of dbt-core and dbt-bigquery so that it
can render a dbt project the way dbt does: how macro names resolve, how
adapter.dispatch searches packages, how generic test arguments are rendered,
and how seed column types are inferred. These were written by reading the
source of:

  dbt-core       https://github.com/dbt-labs/dbt-core       Apache License 2.0
  dbt-adapters   https://github.com/dbt-labs/dbt-adapters   Apache License 2.0
                 (dbt-bigquery)

Copyright dbt Labs, Inc. The regular expression that decides which test
arguments are rendered as Jinja is taken from dbt-core's
dbt/clients/jinja.py. No other dbt code is included; at run time dbt2dataform
uses the dbt installation the user provides.

The helper that dbt2dataform writes into every converted project,
includes/dbt2dataform.js, is licensed under MIT No Attribution (MIT-0), so
converted projects carry no obligation to this project.

